WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.740
- So big news related to a
possible criminal investigation

00:00:02.740 --> 00:00:04.110
of the Trump organization.

00:00:04.110 --> 00:00:06.580
New York Attorney General
Letitia James announces

00:00:06.580 --> 00:00:08.710
that the Attorney General's
office is teaming up

00:00:08.710 --> 00:00:10.870
with the Manhattan
District Attorney's office,

00:00:10.870 --> 00:00:13.610
run by Cy Vance, to combine efforts,

00:00:13.610 --> 00:00:16.040
and that the Attorney
General's investigation

00:00:16.040 --> 00:00:19.430
is no longer just civil, but
is also criminal in nature.

00:00:19.430 --> 00:00:20.970
Now, the Manhattan
District Attorney's office

00:00:20.970 --> 00:00:23.730
was already engaged in a
criminal investigation.

00:00:23.730 --> 00:00:25.690
You might recall that the
grand jury subpoena went up

00:00:25.690 --> 00:00:28.170
to the Supreme Court
twice where Trump lost

00:00:28.170 --> 00:00:29.440
and the District Attorneys won,

00:00:29.440 --> 00:00:31.600
and they should have access
to all of those records.

00:00:31.600 --> 00:00:33.440
But what is particularly interesting

00:00:33.440 --> 00:00:35.420
is that the New York
Attorney General's office

00:00:35.420 --> 00:00:37.700
is now teaming up with the Manhattan DA.

00:00:37.700 --> 00:00:39.660
That basically doesn't happen.

00:00:39.660 --> 00:00:40.890
That might mean that this investigation

00:00:40.890 --> 00:00:42.670
is getting a supercharge,
or it just might mean

00:00:42.670 --> 00:00:44.940
that the Attorney General's
office wants some of the credit.

00:00:44.940 --> 00:00:47.520
The New York AG tends to
announce more investigations

00:00:47.520 --> 00:00:48.740
than it actually prosecutes,

00:00:48.740 --> 00:00:51.013
so we'll see whether
we see anyone in court.

